@@ -0,0 +1,43 @@
+# Homepage components
+
+Load `components/index.js` once with a module script. No dependencies or build
+step are required. Each custom element clones a shared template into an open
+shadow root. Native links and buttons retain keyboard and browser behavior.
+
+## Content slots
+
+- `coffee-card`: `heading` (use an appropriate heading such as `h3`), default
+  slot (description), and `action` (a native link with a descriptive accessible
+  name, including its visible text).
+- `coffee-hero`: `heading` (the homepage uses `h1`), default slot (description),
+  and `action` (a native link).
+- `grind-navigation`: `brand`, default slot (native navigation links), and
+  `account-action` (an optional trailing link).
+
+```html
+<coffee-card>
+  <h3 slot="heading">House Blend</h3>
+  <p>A balanced everyday roast.</p>
+  <a slot="action" href="/menu/house-blend"
+     aria-label="View Details about House Blend">View Details</a>
+</coffee-card>
+```
+
+Keep slotted elements as direct children. Content stays readable and links
+remain usable if JavaScript fails; the compact menu is only introduced after
+the navigation component upgrades.
+
+## Styling and behavior
+
+Components inherit typography and the existing `--primary`, `--text`, and
+`--accent` tokens, with standalone fallbacks. Additional options are
+`--card-background`, `--button-hover`, and `--hero-image` (a CSS `url(...)`).
+For structural overrides, use `coffee-card::part(card)`,
+`coffee-hero::part(hero)`, or `grind-navigation::part(navigation)`.
+
+The navigation switches to a disclosure at 48rem. Its native button exposes
+`aria-expanded` and controls a panel in the same shadow root. Escape closes the
+menu and returns focus to its button; following a link closes it. Listeners
+are removed on disconnect and restored on reconnect. Resizing retains visibility
+of a focused navigation link. Components respect reduced motion and include
+visible keyboard focus without adding the static hosts to the tab order.
